  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is projected at an angle of $30^{\\circ}$ from horizontal at a speed of $60 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$. The height traversed by the particle in the first second is $\\mathrm{h}_0$ and height traversed in the last second, before it reaches the maximum height, is $h_1$. The ratio $h_0: h_1$ is _________\n[Take, $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ ]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/etAOCiDQKfOgOvWYFgoKPTcbC-L4Em2ttg7_0gne078.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{S}_1=30 \\times 1-\\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 1=25 \\\\ & \\mathrm{~S}_3=30+\\left(\\frac{-10}{2}\\right) \\times(2 \\times 3-1)=5 \\\\ & \\frac{\\mathrm{~S}_1}{\\mathrm{~S}_3}=\\frac{25}{5}=5\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
